      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's important not to give your 14-month-old any sugary liquids, including apple juice, especially when they're experiencing symptoms like yours. Dehydration can be serious, and it’s best to consult a pediatrician immediately. They can provide proper guidance and determine if more urgent medical attention is needed. Meanwhile, try to keep your child comfortable and offer clear fluids like water (if they can manage it safely), and monitor their symptoms closely.",
